From 12c0499057cce19c1ef8449682520354e9273eec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 09:20:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 131/131] dhcpd: wait for link events, undo the lease on link
 down (#764)

dhcpd blocks on netcfg events (a new interface, a link that went up or
down) and keeps a timer only while a link is up without a lease. On link
down it removes the address and its routes (addr/rm); the default route
moves to another lease or, with none left, the name server goes back to
/etc/net/dns and the domain is cleared. A DHCPRELEASE cannot go out
without a link, so the server lets the lease run out. A fixed address
stays. /tmp/dhcpd.status has one line per interface: no link, asking,
no answer, bound <address> via <router>, fixed <address>. Fixes the
address and route that stayed after link down (#763).
---
 dhcpd/Cargo.toml  |   4 +
 dhcpd/src/main.rs | 201 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 190 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

